      "promptEs": "ver/saber + qué, cómo, dónde…",
      "questionEn": "When “what,” “how,” or “where” introduces unknown information inside a larger sentence, does Spanish keep the written accent?",
      "answerEn": "Yes. Keep the accent in qué, cómo, dónde, cuándo, cuál, or quién even when the question is embedded inside a statement.",
      "noteEn": "An embedded, or indirect, question reports what is unknown rather than asking it as a separate sentence. It may have no question marks, but the question word still carries its accent. Compare no sé dónde vive, “I don't know where she lives,” with the relative form donde in la casa donde vive, “the house where she lives.”",
